Notification,srinagar, flr" IZE \ August, 2026.S.O 1)-\ Whereas, the draft of the Occupational Safety, Health and WorkingConditions (Jammu and Kashmir) Rules, 2026, proposed to be made in exercise ofthe powers conferred by sub-section (1) of section 133 and sub-section (1) ofsection 135 of the Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code, 2020(37 of 2020), was published, as required by the said provisions, vide NotificationS.O. No. l2l of 2026, dated 23rd April, 2026, in the Official Gazette, invitingobjections and suggestions from all persons likely to be affected thereby within aperiod of forty-five days from the date on which copies of the Official Gazettecontaining the said notification were made alailable to the public;And whereas, the said draft notification was made available to the public on24n Apnl,2Q26;And whereas, no objection and suggestion was received by this Departmentwithin the stipulate period of forty-five days;Now, therefore, in exercise of powers conferred by sections 133 and 135 ofthe Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code, 2020 (37 of 2020)read with section 24 of General Clauses Act, 1897 (10 of 1897) and in supersessionof the following rules, namely-1. The lammu and lGshmir Building and Other Construction Workers(Regulation of Employment and Condition of Services) Rules, 2006.2. The Jammu and Kashmir Factories Rules, 1972;3. The Contract Labour (Regulation and Abolition) Jammu and KashmirRules,1972;4. The Inter-State Migrant Workmen (Regulation of Employment andConditions of Service) lammu and Kashmir Rules, 1984,5. The lammu and Kashmir Motor Transpoft Workers Rules 1972,except in respect of things done or omitted to be done before such Supersession, theGovernment of Jammu and lGshmir hereby makes the following rules, namely: -CHAPTER.IPreliminaru1. Short title, extent and commencement. - (1) These rules may be calledthe occupational Safety, Health and working conditions (Jammu and Kashmir)Rules, 2026.(2) They shall extend to whole territorial jurisdiction of lammu and Kashmir.(3)TheyshallcomeintoforceonthedateoftheirfinalpublicationintheOfficial Gazette.2. Definitions. - (1) In these rules, unless the context otherwise requires, -
