otherwise and shall be kept available at an office or the nearest convenientbuilding within the precincts of the establishment.(2) (i) in case of manual registers and other records, be legibly enteredin ink in English and Hindi/Urdu or the language understood by amajority of the persons employed;(ii) be preserved in original for a period of one calendar year afterthe date of the last repoft or entry:Provided that when the original record is lost or destroyed before the expiryof one year period, true copies thereof, if available, shall be preserved forthe prescribed period.(4) The record as prescribed under sub-rule (1) and sub-rule (2) shallbe produced, electronically or by registered post, on demandbefore the Chief Inspector-cum-Facilitator or an Inspector-cum-Facilitator or any person authorized in that behalf by theGovernment of lammu and Kashmir.
24. The manner and form of displaying notices under clause (b) of section33.-Every employer shall cause to display at the conspicuous place of theworkplace of the establishment under his control, notice showing the name andaddress of the establishment, hours of work, wage period, date of payment ofsuch wages, details of accident and dangerous occurrence in the establishmentfor the last five years, name and address of the Inspector-cum-Facilitatorhaving jurisdiction to such establishment and date of payment of unpaid wagesto such workers in English, Hindi, or Urdu or in any other official language ofJammu and Kashmir as the case may be.
25. Return, manner of filing the return and periods of filing return toInspector-cum-Facilitator under clause (d) of section 33.- (1) Everyemployer of an establishment shall send annually, electronically or otherwise asnotifled a return relatinq to such establishment in duplicate in Form-IX to theInspector-cum-Facilitator having jurisdiction so as to reach him not later than1st February following the end of each calendar year with a copy to DirectorGeneral, Economics and Statistics, Government of Jammu and Kashmir.
2) Register of accident and dangerous occurrences. -The registersof accident and dangerous occurrences required by sub-clause ofclause (a) of section 33 of the Code shall be maintained in a Form-X.3) Register of leave with wages under clause (a) of section 33. -i. The owner, agent or manager of every establishment shallmaintain in respect of every employee thereof a record ofleave with wages electronically or manually in Form-XI ;ii. The register mentioned in clause (i) shall be preserved for aperiod of two years after the last entry in them has been
