581 0 obj <</Length 2662>>stream
L The occupier of every factory to which this Schedule applies, shall-a. employ a qualified medical practitioner for medical surveillance of theworkers employed therein whose employment shall be subject to theapproval of the Chief Inspector of Factories ; andb. Provide to the said medical practitioner all the necessary facilities forthe purpose referred to in clause (a).IL The record of medical examinations and appropriate tests carried out by thesaid medical practitioner shall be maintained in a separate register approvedby the Chlef Inspector of Factories, which shall be kept readily available forinspection by the Inspector.10. Medica! examination by Medical Officer.-I. Every worker employed in a lead processes shall be examined by a MedicalOfficer within 15 days of his first employment. Such examination shall includetests for lead in urine and blood. ALA in urine, haemoglobin content, stipplingof cells and steadiness test. No worker shall be allowed to work after 15 daysof his first employment in the factory unless certified fit for such employmentby the Medical Officer.II. Every worker employed in the said processes shall b€ re-examined by aMedical Officer at least once in every six calendar months. Such re-examination shall, wherever the Medical Offlcer considers appropriate, includetests as specified in sub-paragraph (I).IIL The Medical Officer after examining a worker, shall issue a Certificate ofFitness in Form XXIII. The record of examination and re-examinations carriedout shall be entered in the Certificate and the Certificate shall be kept in thecustody of the manager of the factory. The record of each examination carriedout under sub-paragraphs (I) and (II), including the nature and the results ofthe tests, shall also be entered by the Medical Officer in a health register inForm XXIVN. The Certificate of Fitness and the health register shall be kept readily availablefor inspection by the Inspector-cum-Facilitator.V. If at any time Medical Officer is of the opinion that a worker is no longer fitfor employment in the said process on the ground that continuance thereinwould involve special danger to the health of the worker he shall make arecord of his findings in the said Certificate and the health register. The entryof his findings in these documents should also include the period for which heconsiders that the said person is unfit for work in the said processes. Theperson so suspended from the process shall be provided with alternateplacement facilities unless he is fully incapacitated in the opinion of theMedical Officer, in which case the person affected shall be suitablyrehabilitated.
Page 99 of 282

