Upto 50 persons 2Between 51 to 100 3101 to 200 3 + 1 for every 50 persons thereafter201 to 400 5 + I for every 100 persons thereafter401 and above 7 + L fot every 200 persons thereafterc. a sumcient number of eye wash bottles filled with distilled water orsuitable liquid, kept in boxes or cupboards conveniently situated andclearly indicated by a distinctive sign which shall be visible at all times.2. Occupationat health centre.-In all the factories carrying out processescovered in Appendix'A there shall be provided and maintained in good orderan occupatlonal health centre with facilities as per scale laid downhereunder-
For factories employing upto workers-a. the services of a qualifled medical practitioner hereinafter known asFactory Medical Officer, available on a retainership basis, in his notifiedcllnic near to the factory for seeking medical help during emergency.He will also carry out the pre-employment and periodical medicalexaminations as stipulated in paragraph 4 of this Part.b. A minimum of five persons trained in first aid procedures, amongstwhom at least one shall always be available during the working period.
